              "metadata": {
                "content": "all music should be stored in music/  folder and .raw format.\nto convert music to Raw format its needed to use audacity \nConvert to RAW (header-less) in Audacity\n\nOpen your audio in Audacity\n\nSet the project/sample rate (bottom-left) to what you need (for A2DP/most music use 44100 Hz)\n\nGo to File → Export → Export Audio…\n\nIn Format, choose Other uncompressed files\n\nClick Configure… / Options…\n\nSet:\n\nHeader: RAW (header-less)\n\nEncoding: Signed 16-bit PCM (typical for ESP32 audio streaming)\n\nExport — Audacity will usually save it with a .raw extension.\n\nTip: You can’t “play” a .raw directly like a .wav because it has no header. To check it inside Audacity later: File → Import → Raw Data…\n\nIf you want a quick command-line alternative (optional)\n\nIf you already have WAV and want raw PCM (16-bit little-endian, stereo, 44.1kHz):\n\nffmpeg -i input.wav -f s16le -acodec pcm_s16le -ac 2 -ar 44100 output.raw\n\n\nIf you tell me your file type (MP3/WAV) and the exact format you want (mono/stereo, sample rate), I’ll tell you the exact Audacity settings for it."
              },
              "createdAt": "2026-02-08T12:54:28.050Z"
            },
